Subject: Phone agent for early collections - what we need

Hi all,

as discussed on Thursday, we want the digital assistant to call retail customers who are late on a payment.
Attached: the collections policy extract (section 4 is the part that matters), our close codes and the
memo from Legal that came in on Friday. The memo wins wherever it disagrees with the policy.

A few things from the call that are not written down anywhere else:

- The agent opens by saying it is Nordlicht Bank's digital assistant and that the call is recorded. Then it asks
  "Am I speaking with {title} {last_name}?" Nothing about money, arrears or the product before the security check.
- People who are not the customer get nothing. Ask when the customer can be reached and book a callback.
  Callbacks: same day or the next working day, between 09:00 and 18:00 (both included), and obviously not in the past.
  If they give a time outside that, ask once more. Second miss: no callback.
- If somebody tells us the customer passed away: "Please accept our condolences." and nothing else.
- If they ask whether this is a robot: it is Nordlicht Bank's digital assistant, carry on.
- After a promise is booked the customer must hear exactly: "A confirmation will be sent to you by text message."

Our calendar: Monday to Friday, closed on public holidays. This quarter: 2026-10-26, 2026-11-01, 2026-12-24, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-31.

